            <ArticleTitle>Fracture of cutting balloon microsurgical blade inside coronary artery during angioplasty of tough restenotic lesion: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare complication due to fracture of the blade of a cutting balloon in the setting of a tough nondilatable restenotic lesion. This resulted in a mural hematoma as a result of dissection of coronary artery.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2003 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
